course: dictionary
lesson: 2616
title: The dermis: the skin's inner layer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dermis is a science word about skin. The clues are in the words around it. «Skin has three main layers: the outer epidermis, the dermis with blood vessels and nerves, and a fat layer underneath.» The words "outer" and "underneath" tell you where the dermis sits: it is the layer between the outer skin and the fat.
explain: The dermis is the thick inner layer under the epidermis. Read the second example: «the outer layer has no blood vessels, so a very light scrape does not bleed.» The outer layer is the epidermis, so the blood vessels must be in the layer below it, the dermis.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The dermis helps you feel touch, heat and pain» still makes sense if you put "the inner layer of skin" in its place. If it fits, you have the right meaning.
fact: The dermis is the thick inner layer of skin, under the epidermis.
fact: The dermis holds blood vessels, nerves, hair roots and sweat glands.
fact: The dermis helps you feel touch, heat and pain, and helps keep your body at the right temperature.
fact: A tattoo's ink sits in the dermis, which is why it stays.
exercise: «Skin has three main layers: the outer epidermis, the dermis with blood vessels and nerves, and a fat layer underneath.» Which layer lies under the epidermis and holds blood vessels? | *The dermis | The fat layer | The outer skin | The epidermis
exercise: The dermis helps you do what? | To see colours | To hear sounds | To make your bones grow | *To feel touch, heat and pain
exercise: Why does a tattoo stay in your skin? | Ink is painted only on the outside of the skin | The ink is in your blood | Ink washes away in the bath | *The ink sits in the dermis
test: Which layer of skin holds nerves and blood vessels? | The epidermis | *The dermis | The hair | The fat layer
test: «The outer layer has no blood vessels, so a very light scrape does not bleed.» Why does the light scrape not bleed? | The skin is made of metal | The scrape is always cold | Blood is too thick to come out | *The outer layer, the epidermis, has no blood vessels
exam: Which of these is found in the dermis? | Bones | The thin outer layer that protects | *Sweat glands and hair roots | Dust
